{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MassTheory.ChargeQuadraticSumRule","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MassTheory.ChargeQuadraticSumRule","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":23,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.ChargeQuadraticSumRule.octet_em_pattern_unique","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.ChargeQuadraticSumRule.octet_em_pattern_unique","kind":"theorem","line":239,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/ChargeQuadraticSumRule.lean#L239-L246","doc":"And the couplings are uniquely determined, so the octet fixes them exactly:\ntwo data, two parameters, no slack left over. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.ChargeQuadraticSumRule.octet_em_pattern_surjective","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.ChargeQuadraticSumRule.octet_em_pattern_surjective","kind":"theorem","line":225,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/ChargeQuadraticSumRule.lean#L225-L237","doc":"**The ansatz excludes no octet electromagnetic pattern.** For *any* target\npair `(u, v)` of the two independent splittings there are couplings reproducing\nit, exhibited as `A = 2u + v`, `B = u − v`.\n\nThis is the file's real octet result, and it is negative: a class that reaches\nevery pattern forbids none, so the quadratic-charge ansatz makes no falsifiable\nprediction on the baryon octet — Coleman–Glashow included. It also shows `A`\nand `B` are *fitted* by the octet rather than constrained by it, which is why\n`qou-bn8e` cannot be closed from this data. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.ChargeQuadraticSumRule.octet_em_map_det_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.ChargeQuadraticSumRule.octet_em_map_det_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":220,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/ChargeQuadraticSumRule.lean#L220-L223","doc":"The map `(A, B) ↦ (a − b, b − c)` has determinant `-1/3`, so it is\ninvertible. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.ChargeQuadraticSumRule.octet_em_gaps","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.ChargeQuadraticSumRule.octet_em_gaps","kind":"theorem","line":212,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/ChargeQuadraticSumRule.lean#L212-L218","doc":"The two independent observable EM splittings, in closed form:\n`a − b = (A + B)/3` and `b − c = (A − 2B)/3`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.ChargeQuadraticSumRule.emMinus","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.ChargeQuadraticSumRule.emMinus","kind":"def","line":209,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/ChargeQuadraticSumRule.lean#L209-L210","doc":"The EM shift of the `Q = −1` U-spin multiplet (`Σ⁻`, `Ξ⁻`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.ChargeQuadraticSumRule.emZero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.ChargeQuadraticSumRule.emZero","kind":"def","line":206,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/ChargeQuadraticSumRule.lean#L206-L207","doc":"The EM shift of the `Q = 0` U-spin multiplet (`n`, `Ξ⁰`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.ChargeQuadraticSumRule.emPlus","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.ChargeQuadraticSumRule.emPlus","kind":"def","line":203,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/ChargeQuadraticSumRule.lean#L203-L204","doc":"The EM shift of the `Q = +1` U-spin multiplet (`p`, `Σ⁺`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.ChargeQuadraticSumRule.pn_sigma_determinant_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.ChargeQuadraticSumRule.pn_sigma_determinant_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":191,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/ChargeQuadraticSumRule.lean#L191-L199","doc":"Made precise: the two configuration-difference vectors are linearly\nindependent, so the two splittings determine `A` and `B` separately. The\ndeterminant `(1/3)(−1/3) − (1/3)(2/3) = −1/3` is nonzero. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.ChargeQuadraticSumRule.sigma_gap_independent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.ChargeQuadraticSumRule.sigma_gap_independent","kind":"theorem","line":183,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/ChargeQuadraticSumRule.lean#L183-L189","doc":"The Σ triplet is **not** degenerate the way the nucleon is: its configuration\ndifference is `(2/3, −1/3)`, which is not proportional to the nucleon's\n`(1/3, 1/3)`. So `Σ⁺ − Σ⁻` together with `p − n` does separate `A` from `B`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.ChargeQuadraticSumRule.coleman_glashow","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.ChargeQuadraticSumRule.coleman_glashow","kind":"theorem","line":165,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/ChargeQuadraticSumRule.lean#L165-L181","doc":"**Coleman–Glashow holds for the ansatz — as an implication, not as a result\nof this file.** For every pair of couplings `(A, B)`,\n\n  `(E(n) − E(p)) − (E(Σ⁻) − E(Σ⁺)) + (E(Ξ⁻) − E(Ξ⁰)) = 0`.\n\nKept only so the specialisation is visibly consistent with the corpus. The\nrelation is already proved from a strictly weaker premise in\n`QOU/Eightfold/ColemanGlashowIdentity.lean` (`coleman_glashow_identity`, three\nfree U-spin shifts, any commutative ring), and `u-spin-coleman-glashow.md`\nalready records the `−0.064 MeV` residual. Do **not** cite this declaration as\nevidence for the quadratic-charge ansatz: by `octet_em_pattern_surjective` the\nansatz reaches every octet EM pattern, so it could not have failed CG. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.ChargeQuadraticSumRule.xiMinus_config_eq_sigmaMinus","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.ChargeQuadraticSumRule.xiMinus_config_eq_sigmaMinus","kind":"theorem","line":157,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/ChargeQuadraticSumRule.lean#L157-L161","doc":"`Ξ⁻ = dss` carries `Σ⁻ = dds`'s. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.ChargeQuadraticSumRule.xiZero_config_eq_neutron","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.ChargeQuadraticSumRule.xiZero_config_eq_neutron","kind":"theorem","line":151,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/ChargeQuadraticSumRule.lean#L151-L155","doc":"`Ξ⁰ = uss` carries the neutron's. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.ChargeQuadraticSumRule.sigmaPlus_config_eq_proton","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.ChargeQuadraticSumRule.sigmaPlus_config_eq_proton","kind":"theorem","line":145,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/ChargeQuadraticSumRule.lean#L145-L149","doc":"`Σ⁺ = uus` carries the proton's charge configuration. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.ChargeQuadraticSumRule.pn_energy_gap","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.ChargeQuadraticSumRule.pn_energy_gap","kind":"theorem","line":136,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/ChargeQuadraticSumRule.lean#L136-L141","doc":"**The nucleon splitting constrains only `A + B`.** Both invariants move by\n`1/3`, so the two couplings enter only through their sum and no measurement of\nthis one difference can separate them. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.ChargeQuadraticSumRule.pn_inter_gap","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.ChargeQuadraticSumRule.pn_inter_gap","kind":"theorem","line":132,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/ChargeQuadraticSumRule.lean#L132-L134","doc":"…and in the **interaction** invariant by `1/3` as well — the same amount. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.ChargeQuadraticSumRule.pn_self_gap","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.ChargeQuadraticSumRule.pn_self_gap","kind":"theorem","line":128,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/ChargeQuadraticSumRule.lean#L128-L130","doc":"Proton `uud` and neutron `udd` differ in the **self** invariant by `1/3`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.ChargeQuadraticSumRule.totalCharge_sq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.ChargeQuadraticSumRule.totalCharge_sq","kind":"theorem","line":121,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/ChargeQuadraticSumRule.lean#L121-L124","doc":"Total charge is not an independent invariant: `Q² = Σqᵢ² + 2Σqᵢqⱼ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.ChargeQuadraticSumRule.energy","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.ChargeQuadraticSumRule.energy","kind":"def","line":117,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/ChargeQuadraticSumRule.lean#L117-L119","doc":"The general quadratic-in-charge energy: `A` on the self term, `B` on the\ninteraction term. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.ChargeQuadraticSumRule.chargeInter","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.ChargeQuadraticSumRule.chargeInter","kind":"def","line":114,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/ChargeQuadraticSumRule.lean#L114-L115","doc":"The *interaction* invariant `Σ_{i<j} qᵢqⱼ` — the one the corpus uses. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.ChargeQuadraticSumRule.chargeSelf","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.ChargeQuadraticSumRule.chargeSelf","kind":"def","line":111,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/ChargeQuadraticSumRule.lean#L111-L112","doc":"The *self* invariant `Σ qᵢ²`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.ChargeQuadraticSumRule.qS","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.ChargeQuadraticSumRule.qS","kind":"def","line":107,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/ChargeQuadraticSumRule.lean#L107-L109","doc":"Strange-quark charge — **equal to the down**, which is why the octet\ncollapses to three charge configurations. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.ChargeQuadraticSumRule.qD","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.ChargeQuadraticSumRule.qD","kind":"def","line":105,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/ChargeQuadraticSumRule.lean#L105-L106","doc":"Down-quark charge. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.ChargeQuadraticSumRule.qU","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.ChargeQuadraticSumRule.qU","kind":"def","line":103,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/ChargeQuadraticSumRule.lean#L103-L104","doc":"Up-quark charge. ","signatureChunk":0}]}